.git
.gitignore
.env
.github
# vendor/ IS part of the build context on purpose: the Dockerfile consumes
# vendor/*.deb (licensed Hopper) and vendor/ida/*.run + *.hexlic (baking IDA in)
# when the matching build arg allows it. Those files are excluded from *git* by
# .gitignore, so they can never be committed or pushed - but the build must see
# them or the documented bring-your-own paths silently do nothing.
# Runtime state does not belong in the image:
vendor/hopper-state/*
!vendor/README.md
!vendor/.gitkeep
work/
targets/
ctf/
config/ida/*.hexlic
config/ida-mcp.json
config/rea.env
docs/
*.md
!vendor/README.md
